course: dictionary
lesson: 13680
title: Inheriting: getting things from those before you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Inheriting» is the -ing form of «inherit». It means receiving something that comes from someone who came before you. The words around it tell you which kind of inheriting it is: money, looks, or a job.
explain: «When Grandma died, Sam was inheriting her old piano.» The clue is «died»: the piano came from someone who had passed away. So inheriting here means receiving something after a person has died.
explain: «Lily is inheriting her dad's curly hair.» Nobody has died here, so inheriting must mean getting a feature from your parents through your body. Check it by swapping in a meaning: «Lily is getting her dad's curly hair» still makes sense.
explain: «Ben is inheriting the messy science project from Mia.» Nothing is being left in a will and nothing is in a body. Ben is taking over a job or a problem from the person before him.
fact: Inheriting means receiving something from someone who came before you.
fact: Inheriting money, a house or things usually happens after someone has died, through a will.
fact: Inheriting features means getting them from your parents through your genes, like blue eyes or curly hair.
fact: Inheriting a problem or a job means taking it over from the person before you.
fact: The forms of the word are inherit, inherits, inherited and inheriting.
exercise: «When Grandma died, Sam was inheriting her old piano.» What does inheriting mean here? | Buying something new from a shop | Losing something in a game | Painting a picture | *Receiving something after someone has died
exercise: «Lily is inheriting her dad's curly hair.» What is Lily getting from her dad? | A new hat | A haircut from the hairdresser | *A feature from her parents, through her body | A gift wrapped in paper
exercise: «Ben is inheriting the messy science project from Mia.» What is Ben taking over? | His own birthday party | *A job or problem from the person before him | A bike from his uncle | A cup of cocoa
test: Tom is inheriting his grandad's blue eyes. What is Tom getting? | A hole in his sock | Lunch money | *Blue eyes from his family | A football
test: Choose the right word: Last year, Anya ___ a house from her aunt. | inherits | *inherited | inheriting | inherit
exam: Which sentence uses inheriting to mean taking over a job from the person before? | *Ana is inheriting the class newspaper from the old editor. | Ana is inheriting a sunny day at the beach. | Ana is inheriting a cold from her friend. | Ana is inheriting a cake from the shop.
